The Cybersecurity Manager will join Sia’s Cybersecurity & AI Trust Business Line in North America, leading client engagements from scoping through delivery and playing an active role in growing the practice.&#xa0;
This role combines hands-on cybersecurity expertise with consulting delivery and business development experience. The successful candidate will manage engagements and teams, build trusted relationships with client stakeholders, and contribute to proposals and offer development across one or more of our eight offerings: Strategy, Risk, Compliance, Operations, Data Protection, Offensive Security, Resilience and Training.&#xa0;
Key Responsibilities:&#xa0;
• Lead end-to-end delivery of cybersecurity engagements, owning scope, quality, budget and timeline, with proactive and regular reporting to clients and to the Senior Manager or Partner.&#xa0;
• Serve as day-to-day client lead, building strong relationships with client-side stakeholders up to senior security and risk leaders, and being recognized as a trusted advisor.&#xa0;
• Work with clients to understand their cybersecurity, risk, compliance and AI trust challenges and shape tailored solutions that address them.&#xa0;
• Lead, coach and mentor consultants and senior consultants on engagements, reviewing deliverables, evaluating achievements and supporting their technical and professional growth.&#xa0;
• Lead the design and writing of commercial proposals and identify and qualify new opportunities within existing accounts and with new clients.&#xa0;
• Support account development and go-to-market initiatives across priority offerings, in partnership with Senior Managers and Partners.&#xa0;
• Manage staffing and resource planning for your engagements, working with the Senior Manager and staffing team to ensure efficient delivery.&#xa0;
• Participate in hiring, career development, performance evaluation and retention of cybersecurity talent, acting as a career coach for a group of team members.&#xa0;
• Stay current with emerging cybersecurity and AI security trends, regulations and threats, and bring them into client work and Sia’s offers.&#xa0;
• Contribute to the team’s internal initiatives (Learning and Development, Squads, Lunch and Learns, Cyber Events) and to the firm’s eminence through articles, white papers, webinars, and representation at professional events and trade shows.&#xa0;
• Prepare and present regular status reports on engagements and business development activities to senior management and stakeholders.&#xa0;
• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity or a related field from an accredited college or university. A Master’s degree is preferred.&#xa0;
• Minimum of 6+ years of experience in cybersecurity within a consulting firm or a cybersecurity solutions, service provider or integrator, including at least 2 years leading engagements, workstreams or teams.&#xa0;
• Demonstrated contribution to business development and client relationship management, including proposal writing and account growth in the U.S. market.&#xa0;
• Strong knowledge of cybersecurity frameworks, standards and regulations (e.g., ISO 270xx, NIST, CIS, NYDFS, FFIEC).&#xa0;
• Deep expertise in at least two of our eight offerings, with experience in risk management, compliance, incident response or security operations.&#xa0;
• Working knowledge of networks, operating systems, cloud (AWS, Azure and/or GCP) and major security technologies such as IAM, EDR, DLP and CASB.&#xa0;
• Relevant certifications such as CISSP, CISM, CISA, CCSP or ISO 27001 LI/LA are highly desirable. High potential candidates without certifications may join our internal Cyber Training program within the Sia Cyber Institute.&#xa0;
• Excellent leadership, communication, writing and presentation skills, with the ability to engage senior client stakeholders.&#xa0;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, and the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines.&#xa0;
Attributes for Success:&#xa0;
• You are a supportive leader who develops others and is eager to share knowledge with colleagues and clients.&#xa0;
• You are intellectually curious, with the entrepreneurial spirit to help develop innovative offers and solutions.&#xa0;
• You thrive on high-stakes subjects and want to take on responsibility quickly within a dynamic, supportive team.&#xa0;
• You are committed to delivering high-quality work while meeting client expectations and deadlines.&#xa0;
Compensation & Benefits &#xa0;
Sia invests in total rewards that support how our people work, live, and grow. &#xa0;
Compensation &#xa0;
• Base Salary: $150,000–$185,000. Actual compensation within this range will be&#xa0;determined&#xa0;based on experience, qualifications, geographic location, and other job-related factors&#xa0;permitted&#xa0;by applicable law.&#xa0;
• Annual Performance Bonus (appraisal)&#xa0;
Benefits &#xa0;
• Medical, dental, and vision coverage
• Company-paid life and AD&D insurance; voluntary supplemental insurance and EAP at no cost
• 401(k) with company match and immediate vesting; HSA and FSA&#xa0;
• College savings and student loan repayment programs
• Paid parental leave
• Generous PTO, nine company holidays, and one floating holiday
• Monthly cell phone stipend
• Well-being and professional development programs
Benefits are subject to applicable plan terms and eligibility requirements. &#xa0;
Workplace
Sia values in-person collaboration. This position is based in our Wall Street office in New York City. Consultants are expected to be on site at least three days per week, whether at a client site or at the Sia office or an approved coworking location. When an engagement requires fewer than three days at the client site, consultants are expected to work from the Sia office for the remaining days. Candidates should live within a reasonable commuting distance of the Sia office
Work Authorization
Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of application and throughout their employment. This position is not eligible for employment visa sponsorship now or in the future.
Our Commitment &#xa0;
At Sia, we believe in fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive culture where our employees and partners are valued and thrive in a sense of belonging.&#xa0;
Sia is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment, including hiring, promotion, remuneration, or discipline, are based solely on performance, competence, conduct, or business needs.&#xa0;

