sr:744000161843579:
Contract Type : W2&#xa0;
Contract&#xa0; Title : Project Consultant/ Senior Product Marketing Manager&#xa0;
Duration: Through June 30, 2027&#xa0;
Hours: 40 hours per week&#xa0;
Compensation : $80–90/hour, depending on skills, experience, and location&#xa0;
Location: Bay Area or NYC; PST hours preferred&#xa0;
About the Role&#xa0;
We’re looking for a Senior Product Marketing Manager to lead go-to-market strategy and execution for a consumer AI product at one of the world’s leading technology companies. You’ll shape how new products and features are positioned, introduced and brought to life across consumer channels. Working closely with product, creative, growth and communications teams, you’ll translate emerging AI capabilities into clear, compelling stories that help people understand the product’s value and inspire them to try it. This role requires strong strategic judgment, excellent writing and the ability to move from planning to hands-on execution in a rapidly evolving product environment.&#xa0;
Impact&#xa0;
• Own end-to-end go-to-market plans for product and feature launches, including audience and competitive insights, positioning, goals, success metrics, asset development and integrated launch planning.&#xa0;
• Tailor marketing support to each launch’s scale and priority, from comprehensive launch campaigns to targeted social, app store and website updates.&#xa0;
• Develop differentiated positioning, value propositions and messaging grounded in consumer needs, product capabilities and business objectives.&#xa0;
• Partner with privacy and legal teams to communicate clearly and accurately about privacy, data access and how the product works.&#xa0;
• Lead cross-functional launch planning across product, design, communications, creators, brand, privacy, growth, paid media, web and insights teams.&#xa0;
• Shape content and creative strategy for app store listings and marketing websites, and provide direction to teams amplifying the product across other channels.&#xa0;
• Use generative AI tools directly to create and iterate on marketing assets, product demos and prototypes.&#xa0;
• Maintain current launch plans, track dependencies and decisions, and drive alignment through shared planning tools and regular go-to-market working sessions&#xa0;
What Success Looks Like&#xa0;
• Launches have clear audience priorities, differentiated messaging, measurable goals and coordinated execution.&#xa0;
• Consumers can quickly understand what the product does, why it matters and how to use it.&#xa0;
• Marketing investment and execution match the opportunity and priority of each launch.&#xa0;
• Cross-functional partners stay aligned on decisions, ownership, dependencies and timelines as product plans evolve.&#xa0;
• Audience insights and launch performance inform ongoing improvements to messaging, creative and channel strategy.&#xa0;
• AI-generated assets and prototypes help teams explore ideas, communicate product value and accelerate execution.&#xa0;
• 8+ years of product marketing experience in consumer technology, ideally with AI-powered products, mobile apps or consumer platforms.&#xa0;
• Proven success bringing products to market and driving measurable adoption, engagement or growth.&#xa0;
• Strong positioning and storytelling skills, with the ability to translate complex technology into clear, differentiated consumer value.&#xa0;
• Excellent writing and creative judgment, including the ability to evaluate messaging and creative for clarity, accuracy and audience relevance.&#xa0;
• Strong analytical skills, with experience turning consumer research, competitive intelligence and performance data into actionable recommendations.&#xa0;
• Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional partners and drive decisions in fast-moving, matrixed organizations.&#xa0;
• Hands-on proficiency with generative AI tools for content creation, visual assets, demos or prototyping.&#xa0;
• Experience with AI product marketing and privacy-sensitive consumer communications preferred.&#xa0;
• Bachelor’s degree preferred.&#xa0;
Work Authorization&#xa0;
Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of application and throughout their employment. This position is not eligible for employment visa sponsorship now or in the future.&#xa0;
Our Commitment &#xa0;
At Sia, we believe in fostering a diverse,&#xa0;equitable,&#xa0;and inclusive culture where our employees and partners are valued and thrive in a sense of belonging.&#xa0;&#xa0;

sr:3743990017009716:
Works as a business-facing, hands-on technical lead who partners directly with internal customers to understand business outcomes, workflows, pain points, data needs, and solution requirements and rapidly translate them into secure, scalable, and supportable technology solutions. Combines senior business systems analysis with software and solution engineering to independently shape, prototype, configure, integrate, test, and, when appropriate, build AI-enabled and conventional applications or partner with other teams for medium to larger scale builds. Partners closely with BTS colleagues, including Business Solutions Consultants (BSCs), Business Relationship Managers (BRMs), and BTS Compliance, as well as technical vendor partners, and owns the transition of new application builds to BTS support, including operational readiness and success metrics. Uses forward-deployed and iterative development practices to remain close to users, validate requirements through working software, and continuously refine solutions in partnership with business stakeholders and technical teams. Applies practical knowledge of generative AI, agentic AI, automation, data, APIs, cloud services, and enterprise platforms while adhering to architecture, security, privacy, quality, compliance, and software lifecycle standards.&#xa0;
Responsibilities:
• Partner directly with business stakeholders and Business Technology Solutions (BTS) colleagues to understand business objectives, end-to-end workflows, pain points, decision points, data needs, user experience expectations, and measurable outcomes.&#xa0;
• Lead structured discovery and requirements activities; translate ambiguous needs into process models, epics, features, detailed user stories, acceptance criteria, functional requirements, non-functional requirements, data requirements, integration requirements, and traceability documentation.&#xa0;
• Use rapid prototyping, AI-assisted analysis, agentic AI, workflow automation, and other fit-for-purpose tools to validate assumptions, clarify requirements, demonstrate solution concepts, and shorten feedback cycles with users.&#xa0;
• Develop solution options and technical designs covering application components, AI or agent workflows, data flows, APIs and integrations, identity and access, security, privacy, observability, deployment, support, and lifecycle considerations. Evaluate build, buy, configure, and reuse options.&#xa0;
• Personally configure, prototype, code, integrate, test, and troubleshoot applications or solution components when hands-on development is the most effective delivery approach. Produce maintainable, documented work products that can advance to production.&#xa0;
• Coordinate across software engineering, data, AI/ML, architecture, platform, infrastructure, cybersecurity, privacy, quality, compliance, testing, and support teams to resolve dependencies and move solutions from concept through implementation and adoption.&#xa0;
• Maintain a prioritized backlog and iterate continuously with business partners through demonstrations, usability feedback, testing, and release learning. Balance speed with technical quality, risk, scalability, and user value.&#xa0;
• Define and execute testing approaches, including functional, integration, regression, user acceptance, AI evaluation, and production-readiness testing. Verify that delivered capabilities satisfy requirements and intended business outcomes.&#xa0;
• Collaborate routinely with BTS Business Solutions Consultants (BSCs), Business Relationship Managers (BRMs), and BTS Compliance to align demand, priorities, solution direction, and compliance obligations, and engage technical vendor partners to scope, guide, and review their contributions.&#xa0;
• Plan and lead the transition of new application builds to BTS support, including support handoff, runbooks, knowledge transfer, training, service-level expectations, monitoring and alerting, incident, and problem management, and hypercare.&#xa0;
• Define how each launched application will be operationalized, including ownership, release and change management, access management, enhancement intake, lifecycle and retirement planning, and ongoing support and cost considerations.&#xa0;
• Define success metrics and KPIs with business partners (e.g., adoption, usage, performance, reliability, quality, AI output accuracy, user satisfaction, and business value); instrument solutions to measure them, monitor results after launch, and drive improvements when targets are not met.&#xa0;
• Create and maintain required business, functional, technical, and operational documentation, including architecture and design artifacts, interface specifications, decision records, test evidence, support procedures, and training materials.&#xa0;
• Provide technical leadership within assigned initiatives, guide less-experienced contributors, communicate risks and trade-offs clearly, and independently escalate material architecture, responsible AI, security, privacy, compliance, quality, or delivery concerns.&#xa0;
Required:
• Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, Data Science, or a related discipline plus 5 years of relevant experience; or a Master's Degree plus 4 years of relevant experience.
• Demonstrated experience in a hybrid role spanning business systems analysis, solution engineering, software development, technical consulting, product delivery, or similar disciplines.&#xa0;
• Proven ability to lead business discovery sessions and convert complex or ambiguous needs into user stories, acceptance criteria, functional and non-functional requirements, process and data models, and implementable technical designs.&#xa0;
• Hands-on experience building or configuring applications, integrations, automations, or data-enabled solutions using modern development languages, APIs, cloud services, low-code platforms, or enterprise application platforms.&#xa0;
• Practical knowledge of generative AI and agentic AI concepts, including large language models, prompt and context engineering, retrieval-augmented generation, tool use, agent orchestration, evaluation, guardrails, human-in-the-loop controls, and limitations of AI-generated outputs.&#xa0;
• Understanding of software engineering and delivery practices, including Agile product development, source control, testing, CI/CD, observability, production support, secure development, documentation, and software lifecycle controls.&#xa0;
• Experience working with cross-functional technical teams and translating effectively between business stakeholders, engineers, architects, data specialists, security, privacy, quality, and compliance partners.&#xa0;
• Experience transitioning applications or solutions to a support organization and operationalizing them after launch, including ITSM practices, support models, monitoring, and operational readiness.&#xa0;
• Ability to define, instrument, and track KPIs and performance metrics, and to use them to evaluate whether a system meets business needs and to guide continuous improvement.&#xa0;
• Experience working with technical vendors and partners, including shaping requirements, reviewing deliverables, and holding them accountable to quality and compliance standards.&#xa0;
• Strong analytical, facilitation, communication, and relationship-management skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts, solution options, risks, and trade-offs to non-technical audiences.&#xa0;
• Ability to work with a high degree of independence, manage multiple priorities, make sound technical recommendations, and deliver results through influence in a matrixed environment.&#xa0;
Preferred:&#xa0;
• Experience with GxP, validation, responsible AI, data privacy, or regulated software delivery.&#xa0;
• Life sciences and pharmaceutical industry experience, including familiarity with regulated environments and how technology supports drug discovery and development.&#xa0;
• R&D operations experience, including supporting scientific and clinical research workflows, systems, and business processes.&#xa0;
• R&D contracting lifecycle processes, procurement, and vendor management experience.&#xa0;
• Finance experience, including budgeting, forecasting, invoicing, and financial systems and controls relevant to R&D and technology initiatives.&#xa0;
• Lab support services experience, including laboratory operations, instruments, and supporting systems and processes.&#xa0;
​Applicable only to applicants applying to a position in any location with pay disclosure requirements under state or&#xa0;local law:&#xa0;​
• The compensation range described below is the range of possible base pay compensation that the Company&#xa0;believes in&#xa0;good faith it will pay for this role at the&#xa0;time&#xa0;of&#xa0;this posting based on the job grade for this position.&#xa0;Individual&#xa0;compensation paid within this range will depend on many factors including geographic&#xa0;location,&#xa0;and&#xa0;we&#xa0;may&#xa0;ultimately&#xa0;pay&#xa0;more or less than the posted range. This range may be&#xa0;modified&#xa0;in the&#xa0;future.&#xa0;​
