The Manager, Government Pricing Finance leads financial planning, forecasting, analytics, and required price reporting for U.S. Government Pricing programs. The role oversees Medicaid and 340B rate forecasting, Best Price impact assessments, Average Selling Price (ASP) reporting, and the integration of Government Pricing assumptions into annual Plan, long-range planning (LRP), and periodic forecast cycles. The Manager delivers accurate, supportable analyses; translates complex pricing methodologies into clear financial insights; and partners with Finance, Gross-to-Net (GTN), Legal, Pricing, Contracting, Market Access, and other stakeholders to inform business decisions and meet reporting obligations.The position establishes analytical priorities, reviews models and data for accuracy and completeness, and communicates material variances, risks, opportunities, and recommended actions to management. Success requires independent judgment, strong knowledge of government pharmaceutical pricing, disciplined execution of recurring reporting requirements, and the ability to respond to evolving business, legislative, and regulatory needs.
