We have two types of Product Managers within our teams:  Inbound and Outbound &#xa0;
For the application:&#xa0; I f you’re interested in both Inbound and Outbound Product Manager roles, please apply to your top choice only . Your application will automatically be considered for both roles. You are welcome to include your thoughts during the hiring manager notes.&#xa0;
For context: Outbound Product Manager s enable Go-To-Market teams on product innovation and evangelize the product with customers and partners. Considered the product experts, they generally serve as the bridge between the inbound PM and the product marketing team to ensure the product gets to our customers. &#xa0;&#xa0;
For this role: Inbound Product Managers  plan for and develop new products and future releases of a product. They gather feedback to determine the problems we're trying to solve, then generate a product roadmap. They work with various teams such as release management, design, and engineering development.&#xa0;&#xa0;
A few key responsibilities of Inbound PMs include:  &#xa0;
• Set product vision & strategy &#xa0;
• Define the roadmap, requirements & product success metrics &#xa0;
• Develop and test innovative product ideas  &#xa0;
• Work closely with customers to understand their needs and problems to be solved &#xa0;
• Own detailed competitive analysis for their feature/product &#xa0;
Additional possible responsibilities include:&#xa0;
• Support senior program managers and/or product managers across the entire project lifecycle to deliver critical programs for Service Now initiatives.  &#xa0;
• Work and collaborate directly with Product Managers, Product Design, & Development Teams to build new features and improve adoption on existing features. &#xa0;
• Build familiarity with scrum process and willingness to contribute to team deliverables. &#xa0;
• Understand product strategy that sets us up for success as we look to grow to $15B+ in revenue.&#xa0;
• Research and collect product requirements from key buyer audiences and end-users to determine areas of opportunity for product enhancements.&#xa0;
• Oversee the product or project timeline, deadlines, milestones as it is being built by development/engineering and communicate with stakeholders to keep them updated. &#xa0;
• Contribute to the complete product lifecycle, from researching market needs and competition, analyzing customer data, writing product requirements, and delivering product features to market.&#xa0;
• Understand the technical and business impacts of product decisions that inform tradeoff decisions to optimize against product delivery and customer value. &#xa0;
Internship location may vary based on team growth strategies.
Required Qualifications
• Currently enrolled full-time at an accredited university pursuing an Masters in Engineering, Business Management, Analytics, Computer Science, Information Systems, Applied Sciences, or a related field.
• Graduating May 2028 or later .
• Available to work full-time for a 12-week summer internship .
• 0-3 years of related experience .
• Experience using or evaluating AI to improve workflows, decision-making, problem-solving, automation, or data-driven insights.
• Experience defining product requirements and translating them into a product roadmap.
• Strategic mindset with the ability to balance customer desirability, business viability, and technical feasibility .
• Strong prioritization, problem-solving, and analytical skills, with a data-driven and hypothesis-led approach.
• Deep curiosity about customer needs and a passion for building relationships and delivering high-value solutions.
Preferred Qualifications
• Familiarity with Agile methodologies and the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) .
• Experience collaborating with developers and designers to create compelling customer experiences.
• Demonstrated project management experience through internships, academic work, or personal projects.
